#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "c7cc2dca-cc41-561c-bc48-bbcda272dd71" :question/math-academy-id "e-5792" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "92ac2f4f-d0a5-5ccb-9213-87495927ccb8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8799" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae36425f-5e48-5d4f-8932-3a137c1f94e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084502} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f7b873-fb65-5a93-bedf-1b8d8b3b6cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} + 4x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084503} {:answer/id #uuid "154b65e5-ff43-514f-b226-ec2977e6cc3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} - 4x^{2} - 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084504} {:answer/id #uuid "20ed9f7e-6cd2-5097-861e-c62eb98176d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{3} + 8x^{2} + 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084505} {:answer/id #uuid "291c4f7d-5ed3-53a3-8a1a-28b5bab60d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} + 4x^{2} - 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae36425f-5e48-5d4f-8932-3a137c1f94e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084502} :answer-field/id #uuid "159db6ae-8ceb-5e94-ae54-fd52d97b24a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b7607d8-f365-578e-840c-7619cca90194" :question/math-academy-id "q-104469" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278537} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6e2840-e270-59a4-8d60-c00f23f258ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278538} {:answer/id #uuid "56171563-0615-5fb3-b854-9300e0b02d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278539} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e91be-e836-5466-8026-ab7735b0b298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278540} {:answer/id #uuid "a4bd8db2-376d-5ea8-89f5-d2d2a68965c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278537} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da7061c-555a-54eb-aa9f-d21b81deaa88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54688a98-1474-5993-a7d9-b3966da03d6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17407" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/b771ac7e3d7e724b1eae9ebfc592d36a903a1fc46cc2aac5a55ea9517dc2ce12.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+9x-4{x}^{2}-36 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36.$"}]}
